00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:04.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  in the temple  at the heart of leicester's indian  community they pray  here the crisis that's unfolding  thousands of miles away feels  unbearably close to home  everyone is worried about someone for  syrendra who's a student here in  leicester  the fear is for his mum  he calls her twice a day anxious to  check  she doesn't have symptoms  since his dad died she's lived on her  own in a remote village where the virus  is spreading every morning and every  night i call her  he told me he hasn't been able to visit  her for over a year  and wishes he could be there now who can  look after her if if she got corona  who can take her to the hospital people  are scared now because there is no  oxygen the  hospital is full so all the people  are scared the community in leicester  have already  raised thousands of pounds to help  establish a field hospital  and send oxygen to areas most in need  this city has felt the terrible impact  of covid  a spike in cases here last year has left  many families grieving  so this is a family photo and this is my  father who passed away  last year sanjeev was also  seriously ill with the virus his  experience  makes him fearful for relatives in india  myself and my father ended up in  hospital in critical care  and unfortunately my father didn't make  it out  when i was ill the only treatment there  was that telomere on his oxygen  understanding that whatever other  facilities you've got if you haven't got  oxygen supplies  then your chances of survival are much  more slim  people here feel helpless as they wait  for news they can  only hope that better times are coming  becky johnson  sky news in leicester

